    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federation of seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> formed in 1971–1972 from the British-protected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, with Abu Dhabi as its capital.</li><li>Abu Dhabi's oil and Dubai's ports, airline and free zones made it a global hub of trade, finance and aviation.</li><li>Since the 2010s it has acted as an assertive regional power, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-accords">Abraham Accords</a> with Israel in 2020.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The UAE's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirates-mars-mission">Hope probe</a>, which entered orbit around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mars-mythology">Mars</a> in February 2021, was the first interplanetary mission by an Arab country.</p></aside>
    </section>

